  "stateNote": "Cook the fish and build the broth: Place 1 kilograms fresh catfish (or chicken/goat meat), cleaned and cut and 150 grams stockfish (panla), soaked and cleaned in a pot. Add enough water to cover. Add 1 tablespoons ogiri okpei (fermented locust bean paste), 1 teaspoons ehuru (African nutmeg), ground, blended 3 scotch bonnet pepper (rodo), and remaining 1 onion. Bring to a boil on medium heat and cook until the fish is just tender do not overcook catfish or it will fall apart.",
